Z||000000||GTMike||11-24-2001||12:42 PM||||i replaced my clutch yesterday and when i got it all back together     i though to myself i didn't find a return spring for the clutch arm to pull the throwout bearing back. is there one?   there is a posibility tht it went flying when i pulled the tranny off.    if there is one where does it go?<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-24-2001||12:49 PM||||If the TO bearing was installed correctly then the lever action of the fork will pull it back.....there is no spring.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||11-24-2001||01:12 PM||||Nope, no spring. You didn't lose it 'cuz it wasn't there to lose.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
